# Task 03 — Equal-Height Cards

**Category:** Layout & Structure
**Difficulty:** above-average
**Style school:** Corporate SaaS

## The problem

Cards sitting side by side with uneven content lengths, where each card's
footer (a button, in this case) must still line up across all cards.

## Constraints

- No JavaScript height calculation of any kind — pure CSS only.

## Key implementation decisions

- Each `<article>` card is `flex flex-col`, and the description paragraph
  inside it gets `flex-1`. This makes the paragraph absorb all the leftover
  vertical space inside its own card, pushing the button to the bottom
  regardless of how long or short the description text is.
- The three cards are equal height for free: they're grid items in the same
  row, and CSS Grid stretches items in a row to match the tallest one by
  default — no extra utility needed for that part.
- Colors come entirely from the `brand-*` / `neutral-*` token scale.

